    "importance": "major",
    "summary": "Added paid-only `inferenceport-ai/lightning-text-v2` and `inferenceport-ai/lightning-text-v2.1` with text and image input, JSON output, and tool calling. Both route directly to InferencePort without a fallback; InferencePort serves them through Groq using gpt-oss-20b for v2 and Qwen3.8 27B for v2.1 in testing. Billing is per million input and output tokens, with reasoning tokens charged at the output rate. Provider-only billing metadata is filtered from non-streamed responses, streamed chunks, and cached replays. The sub-processor page now lists InferencePort among gateways that pass requests to a model host. Testing found that v2.1 returned 502 on 3 of 26 direct calls, 20 parallel calls took 4–7 seconds rather than about 1 second, and vague JSON prompts could trigger Groq validation errors returned as uncharged 400s.",
